# Any env file carrying a suffix AFTER `.local` — e.g. neutralising a pulled
# Vercel production env by renaming `.env.production.local` to
# `.env.production.local.DISABLED-for-local-walk`. Every rule above anchors on a
# `.local` ENDING, so such a rename silently drops out of coverage and the file
# reappears as untracked with live production credentials in it. The trailing `*`
# keeps it ignored whatever suffix is appended.
.env*.local*

# Phase 31 — reconciliation dry-run reports (contain live client data, never commit)
.reconcile/

# AI tooling scaffolding — per-developer, generated by skill installers
# (ReUI skill writes into each of these; .claude/worktrees holds live git worktrees).
